From f1ab7fe13895cf8520701b14943de3128b6ab6c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:10:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: FCA11-long driver cut re-arms on the first clean
 frame after the resume grant (G9b, drive-14)

The panda's G9 driver-input latch (hyundai_fca11_long_driver_cut) re-armed on the openpilot resume edge
(controls_allowed rising), but it cleared the latch DIRECTLY on that edge and then re-set it in the SAME
rx call whenever a driver input was still held at that instant. Granting controls in pedal mode needs the
brake released (hyundai_common.h, hyundai_gas_interceptor_pause_button_check) but NOT the gas, so engaging
with the foot still on the gas latched the cut for the whole engagement: on routes 0000014a/0000014b (build
adurham/dev 37bf708bee) 7 of 16 engagements were granted with gas_raw > 420 (574/748/731/739...), the latch
stayed latched for up to 24.7 s, closed hyundai_fca11_long_window_ok() and refused EVERY actuating FCA11
frame - 753 of 755 refused frames on both drives, 7 dead episodes, only 37.5 % of braking frames reached
the ESC. Python never latched (it only latches gas while longActive, and openpilot holds longActive False
with the gas pressed), so the car layer believed the window was open and sent 116 frames the panda refused.

Fix (state exactly what changed and why):
  - on controls_allowed rising the edge now only ARMS a re-arm (hyundai_fca11_long_driver_cut_pending);
  - each rx frame, a live driver input (brake / gas / gear != D) sets the latch as before; otherwise the
    first CLEAN engaged frame clears the latch and consumes the pending re-arm;
  - the SET is kept BEFORE the clear, so a driver input ON the grant frame still wins that frame;
  - the clear is gated on controls_allowed ("after engaging"), so a clean frame while disengaged does not
    re-arm and a cut carried across a mid-drive re-init still refuses until a genuine resume edge;
  - an unconsumed pending re-arm is dropped on any disengage, so a re-arm must be earned inside the same
    engagement;
  - pedal-fault and camera-owns stay in hyundai_fca11_long_cut, hard-latched for the whole arm (unchanged).

Semantics: the gate that re-arms the latch is LEVEL-triggered on the live driver input at the grant. A gas
reading that has ALREADY fallen below the threshold is not re-latched - it re-arms on the first clean frame
(matching stock Hyundai SCC override behaviour: the override ends when the pedal is released, not when the
car re-engages). A pedal still over threshold keeps re-latching every frame, exactly as today. Brake, gear
and camera cuts are untouched in severity: the live window still carries !brake_pressed && !gas_pressed &&
gear D on every actuating frame, so the driver always cuts the CURRENT episode immediately.

Python mirror (opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/fca11_long.py): the car layer must be a strict subset of the
panda. blocked_until_resume is split into _driver_cut (brake/gas/gear; re-arms on the CC.enabled rising edge,
clears on the first clean engaged frame) and _hard_cut (camera hand-back / pedal fault; not re-armed), OR'd
back into blocked_until_resume so every consumer is unchanged.

Tests (test_hyundai.py, class TestHyundaiFca11LongSafety; test_fca11_long.py, class TestG9bDriverCutRearm):
  panda: test_driver_input_released_within_the_engagement_rearms_gas (the drive-14 root cause: engage with
  the gas held, release mid-engagement -> accepted from the release frame), the amended
  test_driver_input_on_the_grant_frame_still_cuts_then_rearms_on_release (refused on the held frame,
  accepted on the first clean frame), test_engage_with_gas_still_held_is_refused,
  test_engage_with_brake_held_is_refused, test_engage_with_gear_not_d_is_refused,
  test_camera_owns_hard_latched_across_gas_release; the G9 R7-B set (override->resume->ACCEPTED per source,
  the mid-drive-re-init discriminator, pedal-fault/camera-owns survive resume) still passes.
  FALSIFIABLE CONTRAST: test_driver_input_released_within_the_engagement_rearms_gas,
  test_driver_input_on_the_grant_frame_still_cuts_then_rearms_on_release and
  test_engage_with_gear_not_d_is_refused FAIL on the shipped rule (base + 0022..0026) and PASS here;
  the four required "must stay refused" conditions pass on BOTH rules.
  python: 6 mirror tests (rearm on gas-just-released, gas-still-held stays latched, gear re-arm, camera hard,
  no auto-resume without an edge, disengage abandons a pending re-arm); 4 FAIL on the shipped car layer.

Firmware: this is a COMPILED-C change (hyundai.h is in the panda safety core), so CI will rebuild and
re-sign the H7 to a NEW binary (series sha changes -> FW_NEEDED=true). Flashing is a separate, explicit
owner decision and this patch does not change the shipped device build (dev 37bf708bee stays as-is).
